{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/intersectional-discrimination",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "intersectional discrimination"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A form of discrimination in which multiple protected characteristics — such as sex, gender, race, ethnicity, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation — interact in a manner that produces qualitatively distinct and compounded disadvantages."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "These disadvantages cannot be fully understood, proven, or remedied by isolating each ground of discrimination and examining it independently. In particular, legal systems structured around single-axis analysis (e.g., discrimination based solely on gender or solely on race) risk excluding or under-protecting those whose experiences do not fit neatly within one category."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "6.3.6"
  ],
  "broader": {
